#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:2
msgid "_<start>_ and _<end>_ can take one of these forms:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:4
msgid "_<number>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:7
msgid ""
"If _<start>_ or _<end>_ is a number, it specifies an absolute line number "
"(lines count from 1)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:10
msgid "`/<regex>/`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:17
msgid ""
"This form will use the first line matching the given POSIX _<regex>_. If "
"_<start>_ is a regex, it will search from the end of the previous `-L` "
"range, if any, otherwise from the start of file.  If _<start>_ is "
"`^/<regex>/`, it will search from the start of file.  If _<end>_ is a regex, "
"it will search starting at the line given by _<start>_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:20
msgid "`+<offset>` or `-<offset>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:23
msgid ""
"This is only valid for _<end>_ and will specify a number of lines before or "
"after the line given by _<start>_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/line-range-format.adoc:32
msgid ""
"If `:<funcname>` is given in place of _<start>_ and _<end>_, it is a regular "
"expression that denotes the range from the first funcname line that matches "
"_<funcname>_, up to the next funcname line. `:<funcname>` searches from the "
"end of the previous `-L` range, if any, otherwise from the start of "
"file. `^:<funcname>` searches from the start of file. The function names are "
"determined in the same way as `git diff` works out patch hunk headers (see "
"'Defining a custom hunk-header' in linkgit:gitattributes[5])."
msgstr ""
